[2026-03-15T08:39:03.940Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H1LaYDMjrRhq2jgWkmtY9a","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's the complete reference:\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nCreate an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to the cloud |\n| `list` | Show all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login` / `logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Display CLI and browser version info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for debugging |\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\n**Record a session:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload when ready:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Server Integration\n\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\nFor detailed options on any command, use the `-h` or `--help` flag."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c55d401-a852-4118-8076-86af31e25399","uuid":"004f8fed-05ef-4762-b693-07196d24947c","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's the complete reference:\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall globally via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun:\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n## Authentication\n\nCreate an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `record [url]` | Launch Replay Browser and record a session |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Upload recordings to the cloud |\n| `list` | Show all local recordings |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Delete recordings locally |\n| `login` / `logout` | Manage account access |\n| `info` | Display CLI and browser version info |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Upload source maps for debugging |\n\n## Basic Workflow\n\n**Record a session:**\n```sh\nreplayio record https://myapp.com\n```\n\n**Upload when ready:**\n```sh\nreplayio upload <recording-id>\n```\n\n## MCP Server Integration\n\nInstall the Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using the provided configuration with your `REPLAY_API_KEY`.\n\nFor detailed options on any command, use the `-h` or `--help` flag.","durationMs":3665,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T08:39:05.173Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01APBJEBvRmhLBvXAnC1YLmu","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview Document\n\n**name:** replay-mcp\n\n**description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**allowed-tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Core Purpose\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser activity. Users can \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Methodology\n\nThe document recommends a structured four-step approach:\n1. Frame investigation as a question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Support conclusions with gathered data\n\n## Main Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** (discover what happened):\n- Error tracking, Timeline views, Console/Storage/Network monitoring, React render analysis, Source code inspection\n\n**Explanatory Tools** (understand why):\n- Stack traces and control dependencies, Point descriptions, Element inspection, React component analysis, Expression evaluation and logpoint monitoring\n\n## Technical Concepts\n\nTwo foundational terms describe the recording database:\n- **Point:** Each JS statement execution or significant event\n- **Element:** DOM element reference independent of specific points\n\n## Investigation Tips\n\nThe document recommends prioritizing relevant code discovery, execution verification, and using Logpoint tools to track expression values across multiple executions for identifying unexpected behavior patterns."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c55d401-a852-4118-8076-86af31e25399","uuid":"972906d3-0d10-4ddd-9e9f-c186589f8e18","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview Document\n\n**name:** replay-mcp\n\n**description:** \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**allowed-tools:** Bash(replayio:*), mcp__replay\n\n## Core Purpose\n\nReplay MCP enables investigation of https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser activity. Users can \"explore and investigate the app's behavior as if you are a detective with a time machine.\"\n\n## Key Methodology\n\nThe document recommends a structured four-step approach:\n1. Frame investigation as a question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Support conclusions with gathered data\n\n## Main Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** (discover what happened):\n- Error tracking, Timeline views, Console/Storage/Network monitoring, React render analysis, Source code inspection\n\n**Explanatory Tools** (understand why):\n- Stack traces and control dependencies, Point descriptions, Element inspection, React component analysis, Expression evaluation and logpoint monitoring\n\n## Technical Concepts\n\nTwo foundational terms describe the recording database:\n- **Point:** Each JS statement execution or significant event\n- **Element:** DOM element reference independent of specific points\n\n## Investigation Tips\n\nThe document recommends prioritizing relevant code discovery, execution verification, and using Logpoint tools to track expression values across multiple executions for identifying unexpected behavior patterns.","durationMs":4446,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
