[2026-03-15T08:45:38.456Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7qHHKtJAbvJbuNAA9SCp1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Search Flights API Data Flow\n\nI've traced the complete data flow from the search flights API endpoint through to the database. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. **Frontend Thunk (searchFlights)**\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/flightsSlice.ts` (lines 111-135)\n\nThe Redux thunk dispatches a fetch request to:\n```\n/api/search-flights?origin=<origin>&destination=<destination>&departureDate=<date>&cabinClass=<class>&page=<page>\n```\n\nParameters sent:\n- `origin` - Airport IATA code (e.g., \"SFO\")\n- `destination` - Airport IATA code (e.g., \"JFK\")\n- `departureDate` - Flight date (e.g., \"2026-04-01\")\n- `cabinClass` - Cabin class (default: \"economy\")\n- `page` - Page number (default: 1)\n\n### 2. **API Endpoint Handler**\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/search-flights.ts` (lines 1-62)\n\n**Query Logic:**\n- Extracts URL parameters: `origin`, `destination`, `departureDate`, `cabinClass`, and `page`\n- Calculates pagination: 20 flights per page with `LIMIT` and `OFFSET`\n- Returns a 400 error if `origin`, `destination`, or `departureDate` are missing\n\n### 3. **Database Query**\nThe endpoint queries the following tables with these **key conditions**:\n\n**Main Flight Query (lines 20-39):**\n```sql\nSELECT ... FROM flights f\nJOIN airlines al ON f.airline_id = al.id\nJOIN airports oa ON f.origin_airport_id = oa.id\nJOIN airports da ON f.destination_airport_id = da.id\nJOIN prices p ON p.flight_id = f.id AND p.cabin_class = ${cabinClass}\nWHERE oa.iata_code = ${origin}\n  AND da.iata_code = ${destination}\n  AND f.departure_time::date = ${departureDate}::date\nORDER BY p.total_price_cents ASC\nLIMIT ${limit} OFFSET ${offset}\n```\n\n**Tables involved:**\n- `flights` - Contains flight information with `departure_time` timestamp\n- `airlines` - Joined for airline details\n- `airports` - Joined for origin and destination airport codes (IATA codes)\n- `prices` - Joined for pricing information filtered by `cabin_class`\n\n**Critical Conditions:**\n1. The query uses `oa.iata_code = ${origin}` and `da.iata_code = ${destination}` - matching by **airport IATA codes**\n2. Date matching: `f.departure_time::date = ${departureDate}::date` - **date-only comparison** (ignores time)\n3. Cabin class filter: `p.cabin_class = ${cabinClass}` - **REQUIRED JOIN** (no results if cabin class has no pricing entry)\n4. Results sorted by lowest total price, paginated to 20 per page\n\n**Count Query (lines 42-51):**\nSame WHERE conditions to get total count for pagination.\n\n### 4. **Test Setup & Seed Data**\n**Files:** \n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/test.ts` (test orchestration)\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` (seed data)\n\n**Seed Data Characteristics:**\n- **SFO to JFK on 2026-04-01:** 23 flights in seed data (23 different flights with various airlines)\n- **LAX to JFK on 2026-04-01:** 5 flights in seed data\n- All flights are seeded for **2026-04-01** (primary test date)\n- All flights have prices for **all cabin classes** (economy, premium_economy, business, first)\n- Test database is created fresh for each test run from a Neon ephemeral branch\n\n**Why No Results Could Occur:**\n1. **Missing cabin class pricing** - If a flight has no price entry for the requested cabin_class, it won't appear\n2. **Wrong date format** - If the date string doesn't match exactly (though seed data uses 2026-04-01)\n3. **Wrong airport codes** - If IATA codes don't match exactly (case-sensitive: SFO, JFK, etc.)\n4. **Database connection issues** - If DATABASE_URL env var isn't set correctly\n5. **Seed data not executed** - If truncateAndSeed() fails during test setup\n6. **Database initialization failure** - If schema creation fails before seeding\n\n### Key Files for Debugging\n\n- **API endpoint:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/search-flights.ts`\n- **Redux slice:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/flightsSlice.ts`\n- **Database schema:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts`\n- **Seed data:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- **Test orchestration:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/test.ts`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a82e71ee65bf18228 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 53442\ntool_uses: 21\nduration_ms: 29868</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c55d401-a852-4118-8076-86af31e25399","uuid":"79e96a57-d0ba-40dd-a438-9cd8603805d0","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/GoogleFlights, I need to understand why the search flights API returns no results. \n\n1. Find the searchFlights thunk in src/slices/flightsSlice.ts - what API endpoint does it call?\n2. Find the corresponding netlify function that handles the search-flights API endpoint\n3. Check the database query - what table does it query and what are the conditions?\n4. Look for any test setup or seed data configuration\n\nI need to understand the full data flow from the search to the database query.","agentId":"a82e71ee65bf18228","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Summary: Search Flights API Data Flow\n\nI've traced the complete data flow from the search flights API endpoint through to the database. Here's what I found:\n\n### 1. **Frontend Thunk (searchFlights)**\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/flightsSlice.ts` (lines 111-135)\n\nThe Redux thunk dispatches a fetch request to:\n```\n/api/search-flights?origin=<origin>&destination=<destination>&departureDate=<date>&cabinClass=<class>&page=<page>\n```\n\nParameters sent:\n- `origin` - Airport IATA code (e.g., \"SFO\")\n- `destination` - Airport IATA code (e.g., \"JFK\")\n- `departureDate` - Flight date (e.g., \"2026-04-01\")\n- `cabinClass` - Cabin class (default: \"economy\")\n- `page` - Page number (default: 1)\n\n### 2. **API Endpoint Handler**\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/search-flights.ts` (lines 1-62)\n\n**Query Logic:**\n- Extracts URL parameters: `origin`, `destination`, `departureDate`, `cabinClass`, and `page`\n- Calculates pagination: 20 flights per page with `LIMIT` and `OFFSET`\n- Returns a 400 error if `origin`, `destination`, or `departureDate` are missing\n\n### 3. **Database Query**\nThe endpoint queries the following tables with these **key conditions**:\n\n**Main Flight Query (lines 20-39):**\n```sql\nSELECT ... FROM flights f\nJOIN airlines al ON f.airline_id = al.id\nJOIN airports oa ON f.origin_airport_id = oa.id\nJOIN airports da ON f.destination_airport_id = da.id\nJOIN prices p ON p.flight_id = f.id AND p.cabin_class = ${cabinClass}\nWHERE oa.iata_code = ${origin}\n  AND da.iata_code = ${destination}\n  AND f.departure_time::date = ${departureDate}::date\nORDER BY p.total_price_cents ASC\nLIMIT ${limit} OFFSET ${offset}\n```\n\n**Tables involved:**\n- `flights` - Contains flight information with `departure_time` timestamp\n- `airlines` - Joined for airline details\n- `airports` - Joined for origin and destination airport codes (IATA codes)\n- `prices` - Joined for pricing information filtered by `cabin_class`\n\n**Critical Conditions:**\n1. The query uses `oa.iata_code = ${origin}` and `da.iata_code = ${destination}` - matching by **airport IATA codes**\n2. Date matching: `f.departure_time::date = ${departureDate}::date` - **date-only comparison** (ignores time)\n3. Cabin class filter: `p.cabin_class = ${cabinClass}` - **REQUIRED JOIN** (no results if cabin class has no pricing entry)\n4. Results sorted by lowest total price, paginated to 20 per page\n\n**Count Query (lines 42-51):**\nSame WHERE conditions to get total count for pagination.\n\n### 4. **Test Setup & Seed Data**\n**Files:** \n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/test.ts` (test orchestration)\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` (seed data)\n\n**Seed Data Characteristics:**\n- **SFO to JFK on 2026-04-01:** 23 flights in seed data (23 different flights with various airlines)\n- **LAX to JFK on 2026-04-01:** 5 flights in seed data\n- All flights are seeded for **2026-04-01** (primary test date)\n- All flights have prices for **all cabin classes** (economy, premium_economy, business, first)\n- Test database is created fresh for each test run from a Neon ephemeral branch\n\n**Why No Results Could Occur:**\n1. **Missing cabin class pricing** - If a flight has no price entry for the requested cabin_class, it won't appear\n2. **Wrong date format** - If the date string doesn't match exactly (though seed data uses 2026-04-01)\n3. **Wrong airport codes** - If IATA codes don't match exactly (case-sensitive: SFO, JFK, etc.)\n4. **Database connection issues** - If DATABASE_URL env var isn't set correctly\n5. **Seed data not executed** - If truncateAndSeed() fails during test setup\n6. **Database initialization failure** - If schema creation fails before seeding\n\n### Key Files for Debugging\n\n- **API endpoint:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/search-flights.ts`\n- **Redux slice:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/flightsSlice.ts`\n- **Database schema:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts`\n- **Seed data:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts`\n- **Test orchestration:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/test.ts`"}],"totalDurationMs":29868,"totalTokens":53442,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1915,"cache_read_input_tokens":50251,"output_tokens":1273,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1915},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
